From: kadaxo <105596590+kadaxo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Compile the scanner against the installed flex's FlexLexer.h

The bundled FlexLexer.h is from flex 2.6.4. Scanners generated by newer
flex (2.6.15 from Homebrew) declare members it lacks, so the build failed
with "out-of-line definition of 'yyread' does not match any declaration".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -45,7 +45,14 @@ bison_target(
 add_flex_bison_dependency(lexer parser)
 
 include_directories(${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR})
-include_directories(dependencies/libraries/flex/include)
+# The scanner flex generates only compiles against the FlexLexer.h of the
+# same flex version, so use the installed flex's header when CMake finds
+# it and fall back to the bundled copy (flex 2.6.4) otherwise
+if (FLEX_INCLUDE_DIRS AND EXISTS "${FLEX_INCLUDE_DIRS}/FlexLexer.h")
+    include_directories(${FLEX_INCLUDE_DIRS})
+else ()
+    include_directories(dependencies/libraries/flex/include)
+endif ()
 include_directories(include)
 
 # Aim for C++17's filesystem first, fallback on boost
-- 
